Age Distribution
The age distribution of the West Edge/Downtown differs from that of Cheyenne and Laramie County.
The median age in the West Edge/Downtown is higher than the city and county, partially because the
share of the population aged seventeen or under (12.1%) is about half that of the city and county.
Over 21% of the West Edge/Downtown population is a Millennial (aged 25‐34), a much higher
percentage than Cheyenne (15%) and Laramie County (14%). Almost 44% of the West Edge population
is between the ages of 35 and 64. About 37% of the Cheyenne and Laramie County population is in
this age group.

